
# Specification Task Execution Rule

This rule defines the process for executing tasks from the implementation plan, ensuring accuracy, focus, and user control during task execution.

1. Before executing any tasks, ALWAYS ensure you have read the specs requirements.md, design.md, and tasks.md files. Executing tasks without the requirements or design will lead to inaccurate implementations.
2. Look at the task details in the task list.
3. If the requested task has sub-tasks, always start with the sub-tasks.
4. Only focus on ONE task at a time. Do not implement functionality for other tasks.
5. Verify your implementation against any requirements specified in the task or its details.
6. Once you complete the requested task, stop and let the user review. DO NOT just proceed to the next task in the list.
7. If the user doesn't specify which task they want to work on, look at the task list for that spec and make a recommendation on the next task to execute.
8. Remember, it is VERY IMPORTANT that you only execute one task at a time. Once you finish a task, stop. Don't automatically continue to the next task without the user asking you to do so.
9. After completing any task or sub-task, the agent MUST update the corresponding checkbox in `PROJECT_ROOT/specs/{feature_name}/tasks.md` to reflect its status before proceeding or asking for user review.
10. After completing and marking a sub-task as complete, the agent SHOULD immediately proceed to implement the next sub-task in sequence, only pausing for user review after each sub-task is finished.

## Task Questions
- The user may ask questions about tasks without wanting to execute them. Don't always start executing tasks in cases like this.
- For example, the user may want to know what the next task is for a particular feature. In this case, just provide the information and don't start any tasks.
7. If the user doesn't specify which task they want to work on, look at the task list for that spec and make a recommendation on the next task to execute.
8. Remember, it is VERY IMPORTANT that you only execute one task at a time. Once you finish a task, stop. Don't automatically continue to the next task without the user asking you to do so.

